@startuml Order Processing Flow
title Complete Order Processing with Authentication

actor Customer
participant Portal as "Customer Portal"
participant AuthService as "AuthService"
participant Session as "Session Manager"
participant Controller as "OrderController"
participant Service as "OrderService"
participant Trigger as "OrderItemTriggerHandler"
participant Database as "Salesforce DB"

== Authentication ==
Customer -> Portal: Access e-commerce portal
Portal -> Customer: Show login options (B2B/B2C)

alt B2B Login
    Customer -> Portal: B2B credentials
    Portal -> AuthService: authenticateB2B(credentials)
    AuthService -> Database: Validate User__c + Account
else B2C Login
    Customer -> Portal: B2C credentials
    Portal -> AuthService: authenticateB2C(credentials)
    AuthService -> Database: Validate B2CUser__c
end

AuthService -> Session: Create authenticated session
Session --> AuthService: JWT token + user context
AuthService --> Portal: Auth success + user profile
Portal --> Customer: Welcome + personalized dashboard

== Browse & Add to Cart ==
Customer -> Portal: Browse products
Portal -> Database: Load Product__c with pricing
Database --> Portal: Product catalog

alt B2B Customer
    Portal -> Database: Apply account-specific pricing
    Database --> Portal: B2B discounted prices
else B2C Customer
    Portal -> Database: Standard retail pricing
end

Customer -> Portal: Add products to cart
Portal -> Session: Store cart in session
Session --> Portal: Cart updated

== Place Order ==
Portal -> Controller: createOrder(cartData)
Controller -> Service: processOrder(orderData)

== Validate Stock ==
Service -> Database: SELECT Stock__c FROM Product__c WHERE Id IN :productIds
Database --> Service: Stock levels

alt Insufficient stock
    Service --> Controller: StockException
    Controller --> Portal: Error message
    Portal --> Customer: "Out of stock" message
else Sufficient stock
    Service -> Database: INSERT Order__c
    Service -> Database: INSERT OrderItem__c[]
    Database --> Service: Order created
end

== Trigger Processing ==
Trigger -> Database: SELECT Product__c FROM OrderItem__c WHERE Order__c = :newOrderId
Database --> Trigger: Product data
Trigger -> Database: UPDATE Product__c SET Stock__c = Stock__c - quantity
Database --> Trigger: Stock updated

== Calculate Totals ==
Service -> Database: Calculate order totals with taxes
Database --> Service: Order totals
Service -> Database: UPDATE Order__c SET TotalAmount__c, TaxAmount__c
Database --> Service: Updated

Service --> Controller: OrderResponse
Controller --> Portal: Order confirmation
Portal --> Customer: Order # + tracking info
@enduml